#
# Conformance case: characteristic/transitive-closure
# Property-characteristic enforcement (H4) — transitivity closure.
#
# ex:before is typed logic:transitiveProperty. Given ex:A before ex:B and
# ex:B before ex:C, the native characteristic pass must derive ex:A before ex:C.
# The chase seeds only from input.nq; this is the mirror axiom.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/characteristic/transitive-closure/> .

ex:before a logic:transitiveProperty .
ex:A ex:before ex:B .
ex:B ex:before ex:C .
